@startuml Data Flow
!theme plain

title TestCaptive - Data Flow & Processing Pipeline

box "Browser Environment" #LightBlue
    participant "Web Page" as WebPage
    participant "Content Script" as Content
    participant "Background Script" as Background
end box

box "Storage Layer" #LightYellow
    database "Session Files\n(.json)" as SessionDB
end box

box "VS Code Extension" #LightGreen
    participant "Review Panel" as Review
    participant "Code Generator" as CodeGen
    participant "Template Engine" as Template
end box

box "Output" #LightPink
    participant "Test Files" as TestFiles
    participant "Test Data JSON" as TestData
end box

== Recording Phase ==

WebPage -> Content: User performs actions
activate Content

Content -> Content: Capture DOM event
note right
  Event types:
  - click
  - input/change
  - navigation
  - keydown
end note

Content -> Content: Extract element metadata
note right
  Collected data:
  - tag name
  - id, name, class
  - data-testid
  - aria-label
  - placeholder, text
  - xpath
  - position
end note

Content -> Content: Apply deduplication
note right
  Smart filtering:
  - Debounce (500ms)
  - Min interval (100ms)
  - Duplicate check
  - Focus/blur pairs
end note

Content -> Background: Send filtered event
deactivate Content

Background -> Background: Build session object
activate Background
note right
  Session structure:
  {
    id: "session_xxx",
    timestamp: "...",
    events: [...],
    metadata: {...}
  }
end note

Background -> SessionDB: Save session.json
deactivate Background

== Code Generation Phase ==

Review -> SessionDB: Load session
activate Review
SessionDB --> Review: Return session data

Review -> Review: Display events in UI
Review -> Review: User selects framework
Review -> CodeGen: Generate code request
deactivate Review

activate CodeGen
CodeGen -> SessionDB: Read session
SessionDB --> CodeGen: Session data

CodeGen -> CodeGen: Prepare event context
note right
  For each event:
  - event type
  - element properties
  - input values
  - page context
  - navigation state
end note

CodeGen -> Template: Process template
activate Template

Template -> Template: Load framework template
note right
  Templates:
  - selenium_template.py
  - playwright_template.py
  - cypress_template.ts
end note

Template -> Template: Multi-pass processing
note right
  Pass 1: Process outer conditionals
  {{#if (eq event 'click')}}
  
  Pass 2: Process inner conditionals
  {{#if element.testid}}
  
  Pass 3-N: Iterate until stable
  
  Final: Clean orphaned tags
end note

Template -> Template: Apply selector priority
note right
  Priority evaluation:
  1. data-testid ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
  2. aria-label ⭐⭐⭐⭐
  3. id ⭐⭐⭐
  4. name ⭐⭐
  5. xpath ⭐
  6. cssSelector (fallback)
end note

Template -> Template: Replace variables
note right
  Variable replacement:
  {{event}} → 'click'
  {{element.testid}} → 'submit-btn'
  {{value}} → 'john@example.com'
  {{page.url}} → 'https://...'
end note

Template --> CodeGen: Return generated code
deactivate Template

CodeGen -> CodeGen: Extract test data
note right
  Extract from input events:
  {
    "input-first-name": "John",
    "input-email": "john@example.com",
    ...
  }
end note

CodeGen -> TestFiles: Write test file
CodeGen -> TestData: Write test_data.json
deactivate CodeGen

== Execution Phase (Future) ==

TestFiles -> TestFiles: Run in framework
note right
  Framework execution:
  - pytest (Selenium)
  - pytest-playwright (Playwright)
  - cypress run (Cypress)
end note

TestFiles -> WebPage: Execute test steps
WebPage --> TestFiles: Validation results

note over TestFiles
  **Future Enhancement:**
  Test results feedback loop
  - Capture failures
  - Suggest fixes
  - Auto-update selectors
  - Alert on flaky tests
end note

@enduml
